# Crypto Scanner percentile analysis endpoints
#
# Both endpoints require fresh Telegram Mini App initData from an enabled user:
#   Authorization: tma <window.Telegram.WebApp.initData>
#
# Copy http-client.private.env.json.example to http-client.private.env.json and
# replace TELEGRAM_INIT_DATA there. The private file is ignored by Git.
# initData expires according to TELEGRAM_INIT_DATA_MAX_AGE (24 hours in the
# example environment), so refresh it from the Mini App when the API returns 401.
#
# Query rules:
# - Every documented query parameter is required exactly once.
# - Extra query parameters are rejected.
# - period_days: integer from 1 through 3650.
# - percentile: number from 0 through 100.
# - minimum_range_percent: non-negative number.

@symbol = BTCUSDT
@periodDays = 30
@percentile = 75
@minimumRangePercent = 4

### Analyze one active symbol
# Returns its percentile range, candle count, and UTC time coverage.
# Expected: 200. The symbol must match an active symbol exactly, for example
# BTCUSDT. Unknown or inactive symbols return 404 symbol_not_found; incomplete
# history returns 409 insufficient_data.
# @name analyzeSymbolPercentile
GET {{BASE_URL}}/api/v1/analysis/percentile/{{symbol}}?period_days={{periodDays}}&percentile={{percentile}} HTTP/1.1
Accept: application/json
Authorization: tma {{TELEGRAM_INIT_DATA}}
X-Request-ID: kulala-analysis-symbol

### Search all active symbols
# Analyzes every active instrument and returns only items whose unrounded range
# is at least minimum_range_percent. Items are ordered by range descending, then
# symbol ascending. The response also reports matched, analyzed, and
# insufficient-data counts.
# Expected: 200.
# @name searchMarketPercentile
GET {{BASE_URL}}/api/v1/analysis/percentile?period_days={{periodDays}}&percentile={{percentile}}&minimum_range_percent={{minimumRangePercent}} HTTP/1.1
Accept: application/json
Authorization: tma {{TELEGRAM_INIT_DATA}}
X-Request-ID: kulala-analysis-search

### Authentication failure example
# Omitting Authorization demonstrates the canonical 401 unauthenticated error.
# A valid Telegram identity that is not enabled returns 403 access_denied.
# @name analyzeWithoutAuthentication
GET {{BASE_URL}}/api/v1/analysis/percentile/{{symbol}}?period_days={{periodDays}}&percentile={{percentile}} HTTP/1.1
Accept: application/json
X-Request-ID: kulala-analysis-unauthenticated

### Validation failure example
# period_days=0 demonstrates the canonical 400 invalid_argument error.
# @name analyzeWithInvalidArguments
GET {{BASE_URL}}/api/v1/analysis/percentile/{{symbol}}?period_days=0&percentile={{percentile}} HTTP/1.1
Accept: application/json
Authorization: tma {{TELEGRAM_INIT_DATA}}
X-Request-ID: kulala-analysis-invalid
